    "verified_run": 35512293321,
    "operative_contract": "Supersession events are explicit admission audit records, not formal derivations and not proof-budget expenditure. Removed premises cannot become explanation support. Legacy four-item unpack alone is not a proof-completeness claim."
  },
  "source_trace": [
    "sealed post0022 inference.infer performs bounded admission and also appends an InferenceStep named bounded-correction-supersession to the same list as formal derivations",
    "failed candidate direct_proof.admit preserves input order and exact subject/relation/universal/modality scope; emits old_key/new_key, removed_input_indexes, control_input_index, admission-event-not-formal-proof role and false semantic/answer authority",
    "infer_compatible passes only admitted input rows to build_ledger, constructs steps exclusively from finite ledger.records, returns admission_audit separately in evidence-bearing InferenceResult",
    "InferenceResult.__iter__ yields derived/steps/candidates/status; the historical test run helper discards the result object and therefore does not inspect its explicit admission_audit",
    "reasoning.build_multi_memory_reasoning retains the result object and copies its admission_audit into MultiMemoryReasoningMathState.proof_admission_audit, which survives JSON serialization",
    "select_query WHY uses genuine ledger records and excludes target self-support; gate_compatible projects only formal records for both response and autonomous candidates; admission events never bypass missing provenance or completeness"
  ],
  "diagnosis": "Historical assertion has an obsolete representation/semantic expectation: it requires a premise-admission operation to be emitted as a formal inference step. The correction itself and its typed audit are preserved. No runtime correction is demonstrated necessary for this failure.",
  "why_not_restore_legacy_step": "Doing so would violate the externally verified separation of admission events and formal proof records; existing focused control explicitly forbids this rule in formal steps. The sealed direct WHY implementation is characterized to count that old event as support for the corrected target itself. No new semantic choice or proof route should be invented to satisfy a stale representation assertion.",
  "test_contract_decision": "Migrate the historical correction assertion to the explicit admission audit with stronger typed/provenance/zero-authority assertions. Preserve all original parsed-proposition, correction marker, blue-answer and selection-status checks. Also require no correction event in formal steps/ledger, no self-explanation, and preserved reasoning-state audit. This is a test-contract migration, not weakening correction/provenance safety.",
  "proposed_next_changed_file_scope": [
    "tests/test_v082_hf2_reasoning.py"
  ],
